<title>ROMANIA: Romanian GDP forecasts table by 2000-government.</title>
<headline>Romanian GDP forecasts table by 2000-government.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are forecasts of Romania's gross domestic product (GDP) and its main components until 2000 as released by the government's Economic Reform Council on Monday:</p>
<p>			     1996	  1997    1998    1999    2000</p>
<p>			  (trln lei)	    (pct chhange)</p>
<p>  GDP		    109.5	  -3.0    +2.3    +3.4    +4.0</p>
<p> Industry		 39.4	  -5.0    +2.1    +2.6    +3.2</p>
<p> Agriculture	    21.1	  +2.0    +3.3    +4.0    +4.8</p>
<p> Construction	    7.4	  +0.8    +2.1    +2.5    +2.9</p>
<p> Trade and tourism     9.6	  -4.2    +2.6    +3.6    +4.1</p>
<p> Transport		 7.2	  -5.9    +0.3    +1.9    +2.2</p>
<p> Financial activities  6.1	  +0.4    +2.6    +4.2    +5.1</p>
<p> Other services	 14.6	  -5.7    +3.2    +5.3    +6.2</p>
<p>NOTE: Last year Romania's GDP grew by 4.1 percent, down from 7.1 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>The government also put year-on-year consumer price inflation at 97 percent for this year, 30 percent for 1998, 20 percent for 1999 and 15 percent for 2000. ($=7,122 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
